-- d4_no_infinite_descent: the LIVENESS verdict soundness core, authored in
-- CLEAN's surface language and checked by CLEAN's CIC kernel (so it enters the
-- clean kernel's trust base).
--
-- TY SOUNDNESS META-THEOREM (well-founded-measure liveness principle).
-- TY's enumerator-free liveness verdict discharges progress by exhibiting a
-- `Nat`-valued measure that STRICTLY DECREASES on every step of the run. The
-- soundness meaning of that verdict is exactly: such a measure cannot decrease
-- forever — there is NO infinite strictly-decreasing sequence of naturals. Once
-- that holds, the measure reaches its floor (0 / a target) in FINITELY many
-- steps, i.e. the run terminates / makes progress; that is what the verdict
-- asserts.
--
-- STATEMENT PROVED (raw no-infinite-descent, the STRONGEST faithful form):
--   d4_no_infinite_descent : (f : Nat -> Nat)
--     -> ((n : Nat) -> Nat.lt (f (Nat.succ n)) (f n)) -> False
-- i.e. there is no `f : Nat -> Nat` with `f (n+1) < f n` for every `n`. This
-- is FULLY GENERAL over the sequence `f` (no bound assumed); it subsumes the
-- weaker "bounded finite-descent" form (`(∀ n, f n ≤ k) -> …`), which is the
-- special case where a bound is known.
--
-- The transition-system reading is `d4_wf_measure_liveness` below: for an
-- ARBITRARY state type, an arbitrary run `s : Nat -> State`, and an arbitrary
-- measure `mu : State -> Nat`, no run can have `mu` strictly decreasing at
-- every step. That is the well-founded-measure liveness principle verbatim.
--
-- PROOF: well-founded induction on `Nat.lt` via the prelude's kernel-checked,
-- sorry-free `Nat.accNatLt : (n : Nat) -> Acc Nat.lt n` and the primitive
-- `Acc.rec`. No axioms beyond the foundational prelude; no `sorry`.

-- `NoDescTo a`: no strictly-decreasing sequence can start (at index 0) from the
-- value `a`. The predicate the Acc-induction carries.
def NoDescTo (a : Nat) : Prop :=
  (g : Nat -> Nat) ->
  ((n : Nat) -> Nat.lt (g (Nat.succ n)) (g n)) ->
  (@Eq Nat (g Nat.zero) a) ->
  False

-- Core lemma by well-founded induction (`Acc.rec` over accessibility of `a`).
-- Step case: given a decreasing `g` with `g 0 = x`, the tail `g' n := g (n+1)`
-- is again decreasing, its head `g' 0 = g 1` satisfies `g 1 < g 0 = x` (so it
-- is an `Nat.lt`-predecessor of `x`), and the induction hypothesis at `g 1`
-- rules the tail out — contradiction. The `g 1 < g 0` witness is transported
-- to `g 1 < x` along `h0 : g 0 = x` with `Eq.subst`.
theorem no_desc_acc (a : Nat) (acc : Acc Nat.lt a) : NoDescTo a :=
  @Acc.rec Nat Nat.lt
    (fun (x : Nat) (_ : Acc Nat.lt x) => NoDescTo x)
    (fun (x : Nat)
         (_h : (y : Nat) -> Nat.lt y x -> Acc Nat.lt y)
         (ih : (y : Nat) -> Nat.lt y x -> NoDescTo y) =>
       fun (g : Nat -> Nat)
           (hg : (n : Nat) -> Nat.lt (g (Nat.succ n)) (g n))
           (h0 : @Eq Nat (g Nat.zero) x) =>
         ih (g (Nat.succ Nat.zero))
            (@Eq.subst Nat
               (fun (z : Nat) => Nat.lt (g (Nat.succ Nat.zero)) z)
               (g Nat.zero) x h0
               (hg Nat.zero))
            (fun (n : Nat) => g (Nat.succ n))
            (fun (n : Nat) => hg (Nat.succ n))
            (@Eq.refl Nat (g (Nat.succ Nat.zero))))
    a acc

-- THE THEOREM: no infinite strictly-decreasing Nat sequence exists.
-- Instantiate `no_desc_acc` at the accessible starting value `f 0` (accessible
-- by `Nat.accNatLt`), with the sequence `f` itself and `Eq.refl : f 0 = f 0`.
theorem d4_no_infinite_descent
    (f : Nat -> Nat)
    (hdec : (n : Nat) -> Nat.lt (f (Nat.succ n)) (f n)) : False :=
  no_desc_acc (f Nat.zero) (Nat.accNatLt (f Nat.zero))
    f hdec (@Eq.refl Nat (f Nat.zero))

-- Liveness principle over an ARBITRARY transition system: no run `s` can carry
-- a `Nat` measure `mu` that strictly decreases on every step. The measure
-- sequence `fun n => mu (s n)` is exactly the `f` ruled out above.
theorem d4_wf_measure_liveness
    (State : Type) (mu : State -> Nat) (s : Nat -> State)
    (hdec : (n : Nat) -> Nat.lt (mu (s (Nat.succ n))) (mu (s n))) : False :=
  d4_no_infinite_descent (fun (n : Nat) => mu (s n)) hdec